# Forbidden-pattern list for the pre-commit / commit-msg privacy hooks.
#
# Copy this to  patterns.local  (gitignored) and fill in YOUR machine's real
# values, so they are enforced locally and can never be committed to this public
# repo. One POSIX extended-regex per line; matching is case-insensitive.
#
# ⚠️  ONLY a line STARTING with "#" is a comment. A trailing comment becomes part
#     of the regex and SILENTLY disables that pattern — the hook keeps running and
#     reports nothing. Keep every comment on its own line.
#
# Use SPECIFIC values rather than broad regexes, so legitimate placeholders in the
# repo (documentation IPs, example mounts) don't trip the hook. Generic shape-based
# patterns — private IP ranges, tailnet domains, absolute home paths, attribution
# trailers — are already compiled into _patterns.sh and need no entry here.
#
# Example (each pattern on its own line, no trailing comments):
#
#   my-hostname
#   203\.0\.113\.[0-9]+
#   /mnt/myarray
#   me@example\.com
#   \bmysurname\b
#
# Activate the hooks once per clone:  git config core.hooksPath .githooks
